--   The rounded weight grid eventually satisfies the local small-error condition
-- statement:
--   Write \(a_n=\log n/\log\log n\) and \(L_C(n)=\lceil Ca_n\rceil_+\),
--   where \(\lceil x\rceil_+=\max\{0,\lceil x\rceil\}\). For \(d\ge0\) and \(S,b\ge0\), put
--   \(T_n=S+\sqrt d\,\sqrt{2(b+4)\log n}\) and \(A_n=T_nS+S^2/2\). For any fixed real \(C\), with no positivity assumption on \(C\), set
--   \[
--   k_n=\binom{2L_C(n)+d}{d},\qquad M_n=\lceil k_n n^{16}\rceil_+.
--   \]
--   Then, for all sufficiently large integers \(n\),
--   \[
--   e^{2A_n}\frac{2k_n}{M_n}\le\frac12.
--   \]
